# Named display slots
@scenario tutorial_lesson_32
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/32_display_slots.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt slots]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Let's put two portraits at the same position. Named slots let commands address the portraits individually.
@label compare
> Stack both portraits -> stack
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label stack
[hide ginger]
# region slots
[show ginger guide thoughtful slot=rear z=0]
[show ginger guide confused slot=front z=10]
# endregion
narrator: The confused portrait is in front. Try removing just the front slot.
> Hide only the front slot -> reveal
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label reveal
[hide slot=front]
narrator: The thoughtful portrait is still there. Swap the two z values and replay. The position decides where the portraits go. The slot decides which instance a command addresses.
[jump compare]
@label return_hub
[hide slot=rear]
[hide slot=front]
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_32]
[flag tutorial_done_32]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_7]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Swap the z values, then hide front. What should still happen?
> Hide whichever portrait now renders on top. -> practice_hint
> Remove the front slot even if it renders behind rear. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Layer order and slot addressing are separate; hiding front still removes front.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: Layer order and slot addressing are separate; hiding front still removes front.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the interactive lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: What identifies the front portrait when both use the same position?
> The front slot ID. -> correct
> The centre position alone. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Position is shared. The slot uniquely identifies the visible instance.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: Position is shared. The slot uniquely identifies the visible instance.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
